// Mathematical constants and functions.
//
// A package of its own rather than methods on `float`: a constant has no
// receiver and no arguments, and a zero-parameter static method has neither a
// value to resolve against nor anything to fold, so one survived only where
// the optimizer ran.
//
// The functions -- `sqrt`, `pow` and the trigonometry -- live here too: each
// takes a float without being about one, so a call reads `math.sin(x)` rather
// than as a static method of the type.
